# CONTEXTUAL CORRECTIONS — known traps for this campaign
The following are known mistranscriptions where the WRONG form is also a real English word.
Apply each correction ONLY when surrounding context clearly fits the canonical form.

• Canonical: "Item-Epsilon"
  Commonly mis-heard as: "Item-Epsilone", "Itum-Epsilon"
  When to apply: Always the humming blade, never a generic epsilon.

• Canonical: "NPC-Gamma"
  Commonly mis-heard as: "NPC-Gama"
  When to apply: The gatekeeper; they/them.


